.TH ZVM-CLEAN 1 "October 2026" "ZVM v0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-clean \- remove downloaded ZVM build archives and stale per-shell links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm clean
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove files ending in
.BR .zip ,
.BR .xz ,
or
.B .tar
from the top level of the ZVM base directory.
Installed Zig version directories are not removed.
.PP
Also garbage-collect the dedupe store: files in
.I ~/.zvm/store
whose hard-link count is 1 are no longer linked from any installed version and
are removed. Removing a store file never removes data an installed version
still links to.
.PP
Also remove per-shell links created by
.BR zvm-env (1)
that are more than a week old and whose shell is no longer running.
Only links whose names match ZVM's naming scheme are considered, and links
are removed without being followed, so nothing they point to is touched.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-dedupe (1),
.BR zvm-env (1),
.BR zvm-uninstall (1)
